    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.ofFn#doc\">docs#List.ofFn</a> and lots of <code>coeFn</code> come to mind</p>",
        "id": 578625812,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1773232293
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would also point out that the inequality is a consequence of the following facts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt{a * b} \\leq \\frac{a + b}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0682em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9322em;\"><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"padding-left:0.833em;\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∗</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.8922em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hide-tail\" style=\"min-width:0.853em;height:1.08em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400em\" height=\"1.08em\" viewBox=\"0 0 400000 1080\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin slice\"><path d=\"M95,702\nc-2.7,0,-7.17,-2.7,-13.5,-8c-5.8,-5.3,-9.5,-10,-9.5,-14\nc0,-2,0.3,-3.3,1,-4c1.3,-2.7,23.83,-20.7,67.5,-54\nc44.2,-33.3,65.8,-50.3,66.5,-51c1.3,-1.3,3,-2,5,-2c4.7,0,8.7,3.3,12,10\ns173,378,173,378c0.7,0,35.3,-71,104,-213c68.7,-142,137.5,-285,206.5,-429\nc69,-144,104.5,-217.7,106.5,-221\nl0 -0\nc5.3,-9.3,12,-14,20,-14\nH400000v40H845.2724\ns-225.272,467,-225.272,467s-235,486,-235,486c-2.7,4.7,-9,7,-19,7\nc-6,0,-10,-1,-12,-3s-194,-422,-194,-422s-65,47,-65,47z\nM834 80h400000v40h-400000z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1078em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2251em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8801em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span> (AM-GM inequality, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Real.geom_mean_le_arith_mean#doc\">docs#Real.geom_mean_le_arith_mean</a>)</li>\n<li>the arithmetic mean is smaller than the maximum</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 578630664,
        "sender_full_name": "Joris van Winden",
        "timestamp": 1773233559
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1010614\">Joris van Winden</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/sqrt_mul_le_max.20.3A.20which.20proof.20to.20use/near/578630664\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I would also point out that the inequality is a consequence of the following facts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt{a * b} \\leq \\frac{a + b}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0682em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9322em;\"><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"padding-left:0.833em;\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∗</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.8922em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hide-tail\" style=\"min-width:0.853em;height:1.08em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400em\" height=\"1.08em\" viewBox=\"0 0 400000 1080\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin slice\"><path d=\"M95,702\nc-2.7,0,-7.17,-2.7,-13.5,-8c-5.8,-5.3,-9.5,-10,-9.5,-14\nc0,-2,0.3,-3.3,1,-4c1.3,-2.7,23.83,-20.7,67.5,-54\nc44.2,-33.3,65.8,-50.3,66.5,-51c1.3,-1.3,3,-2,5,-2c4.7,0,8.7,3.3,12,10\ns173,378,173,378c0.7,0,35.3,-71,104,-213c68.7,-142,137.5,-285,206.5,-429\nc69,-144,104.5,-217.7,106.5,-221\nl0 -0\nc5.3,-9.3,12,-14,20,-14\nH400000v40H845.2724\ns-225.272,467,-225.272,467s-235,486,-235,486c-2.7,4.7,-9,7,-19,7\nc-6,0,-10,-1,-12,-3s-194,-422,-194,-422s-65,47,-65,47z\nM834 80h400000v40h-400000z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1078em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2251em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8801em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span> (AM-GM inequality, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Real.geom_mean_le_arith_mean#doc\">docs#Real.geom_mean_le_arith_mean</a>)</li>\n<li>the arithmetic mean is smaller than the maximum</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This is indeed what the proof of <code>sqrt_mul_le_max₃</code> uses.</p>",
        "id": 578631961,
        "sender_full_name": "Tjeerd Jan Heeringa",
        "timestamp": 1773233895
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just one more:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt_mul_le_max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt_le_iff_le_sq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gcongr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 578654312,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1773239001
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hum, I kind of dislike the fact that <code>grw</code> can be used as a replacement for <code>rw</code>. I think it makes proof hard to read. This works just as well:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt_mul_le_max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt_le_iff_le_sq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gcongr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 578684540,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773245715
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh sure, sorry, I was originally going to use <code>grw</code> for something but it didn't work (likely user error).</p>",
        "id": 578712025,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1773252870
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What do people think of a linter that warns when you use <code>grw</code> with an equality/iff lemma? I know it can be convenient to use a single <code>grw</code> call with a combination of equality rewrites and generalized rewrites, but I think that it comes at the cost of readability.</p>",
        "id": 578712643,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773253089
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If it's not expensive to run, then that seems reasonable.</p>",
        "id": 578712727,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1773253119
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is the proposal then that <code>grw</code> shouldn't support equalities at all?</p>",
        "id": 578713197,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773253287
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's not clear to me why we'd want to allow <code>grw [eq1, eq2]</code> and <code>grw [ineq1, ineq2]</code> but lint against <code>grw [eq1, ineq1]</code></p>",
        "id": 578713327,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773253330
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The proposal is that it will support equalities, but with a warning (which can be turned off using a set_option). This will discourage people from writing <code>grw [eq1, eq2]</code> or <code>grw [eq1, ineq1]</code>.</p>",
        "id": 578713693,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773253458
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Personnally I really like putting everything in a single <code>grw</code> when there is at least an equality. <code>grw</code> stands for \"generalized rewrite\" right? So I think it makes sense.</p>",
        "id": 578716414,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1773254406
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it could be reasonable to lint against <em>every</em> expression being an equality and suggesting <code>rw [eq1, eq2]</code> instead</p>",
        "id": 578716719,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773254516
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also agree with the above. Perhaps a warning if you use only equalities (and hence could be replaced with rw).</p>",
        "id": 578716722,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ledvinka",
        "timestamp": 1773254518
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>agreed, I thought the purpose of the linter was only to avoid using equalities alone. It would be silly if we have to turn <code>grw [foo, bar, baz]</code> into<code> grw [foo]; rw [bar]; grw[baz]</code> or else silence the linter.</p>",
        "id": 578719922,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1773255616
    }
]